<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19859" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βῆσσα</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βᾶσσα</span></b> , ἡ, poet. Noun, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wooded
				combe, glen</i>, in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> mostly <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔρεος ἐν βήσσῃς</span>
			in the mountain <i>glens</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.34
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν καλῇ βήσσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.588
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.435
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοίλη δ᾽ ὑποδέδρομε βῆσσα τρηχεῖα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					284
				</span></i>
			: pl. for sg., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν βήσσῃσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					10.210
				</span></i>
			: used also by <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i>, twice by <i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>OC</u>
				673
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Aj.</u>
				197
			</span></i>, and <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				618b24
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>drinkingcup</i> at Alexandria, broader below and narrower
			above, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				11.784b
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
